vaporOS nuttx-apps patch: lua-32bit-typo

Problem:   two bugs keep "Use 32-bit integers and floats" (INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BIT, default y)
           from ever working.
           1. Makefile and CMakeLists.txt test CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BITS (an S too many),
              which never exists, so -DLUA_32BITS is never passed.
           2. Even when passed, Lua 5.4.3 and newer ignore it: luaconf.h hard-codes
              "#define LUA_32BITS 0" (5.4.0 tested defined(LUA_32BITS)).
           Result: Lua is always built with 64-bit integers and doubles.
Evidence:  RP2040-Zero (Cortex-M0+), vlua with the defaults: math.maxinteger is
           9223372036854775807 and math.pi prints 3.1415926535898.
Fix:       use the real option name in Makefile and CMakeLists.txt, and (Makefile only) flip
           the luaconf.h line once after unpacking when the option is on. Nothing else
           that includes lua.h may disagree: vlua and its libraries pass -DLUA_32BITS too.
Upstream:  Part 1 yes (trivial). Part 2 maybe: a sed on a downloaded file is a workaround; a
           proper fix would pick LUA_INT_TYPE/LUA_FLOAT_TYPE some other way.

diff --git a/interpreters/lua/Makefile b/interpreters/lua/Makefile
--- a/interpreters/lua/Makefile
+++ b/interpreters/lua/Makefile
@@ -49,3 +49,3 @@
 
-ifeq ($(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BITS),y)
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BIT),y)
 CFLAGS += -DLUA_32BITS
@@ -82,2 +82,10 @@
 endif
+
+# Lua 5.4.3 and newer hard-code "#define LUA_32BITS 0" in luaconf.h, so -DLUA_32BITS has no effect there
+# (5.4.0 tests defined(LUA_32BITS), where the flag above is enough). Flip the line once, after unpacking.
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BIT),y)
+context::
+	$(Q) if grep -q '^#define LUA_32BITS[[:space:]]*0' $(LUA_SRC)$(DELIM)luaconf.h 2>/dev/null; then \
+		sed -i 's/^\(#define LUA_32BITS[[:space:]]*\)0/\11/' $(LUA_SRC)$(DELIM)luaconf.h; fi
+endif
 
diff --git a/interpreters/lua/CMakeLists.txt b/interpreters/lua/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/interpreters/lua/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/interpreters/lua/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -53,3 +53,3 @@
              -DLUA_PROGNAME=\"lua\")
-  if(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BITS)
+  if(CONFIG_INTERPRETERS_LUA_32BIT)
     list(APPEND CFLAGS -DLUA_32BITS)
